/tmp_output*.csv
code/evaluation/usage_report.md

# --- LLM response cache ---
# NOT committed. It's a generated artifact, and it's stored as a single
# ~139KB JSON line — git diffs line-by-line, so every change would rewrite
# the whole blob, producing unreadable diffs and a fresh 139KB object in
# history on every commit.
#
# The app does not need it: engine/explain.py falls back to
# deterministic_explanation(), so decision_explanation is always sensible
# prose with no key, no quota and no cache. The cache only speeds up repeat
# runs and avoids re-spending quota.
#
# Note: message/image extraction signals DO shift a few borderline
# decisions, so exactly reproducing the metrics in README.md needs either a
# GEMINI_API_KEY or a copy of this cache. See "Reproducing the results".
code/.llm_cache.json

